<h1 class="article-title">Auction Announced for Property at Eksporta Street 3 in the Liepāja Industrial Park</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>As development of the Liepāja Industrial Park continues on the site of the former Liepājas metalurgs steelworks, the Liepāja Special Economic Zone (Liepāja SEZ) Authority has announced an auction for the property at 3 Eksporta Street, located within the industrial park. This is the next step towards involving businesses in the revitalisation and transformation of the industrial area, offering the opportunity to acquire existing production buildings together with the land.</p><p>The Liepāja Special Economic Zone Authority is organising an ascending-bid electronic auction for a newly formed property at 3 Eksporta Street, Liepāja.</p><p>Auction property:</p><ul><li>Address: 3 Eksporta Street, Liepāja</li><li>Land: total area 51,521 m²</li><li>The plot contains buildings, including warehouses of various sizes, a production workshop, a workshop building and other structures.</li><li>Starting price: EUR 680,000.00</li><li>Bid increment: EUR 6,800.00</li><li>Security deposit: EUR 68,000.00</li></ul><p> </p><p>Auction conditions to consider:</p><ul><li>The building(s) must be renovated or reconstructed, and the site improved, within 60 (sixty) months of signing the purchase agreement;</li><li>The buildings must meet the minimum energy efficiency requirements stipulated by the laws and regulations of the Republic of Latvia;</li><li>At least EUR 733,076.85 (seven hundred thirty-three thousand seventy-six euros and 85 cents) must be invested in the auction property.</li></ul><p>The auction opens on 6 October 2026 at 13:00 and closes on 5 November 2026 at 13:00. Bidders may register between 6 October 2026 at 13:00 and 26 October 2026 at 23:59 on the electronic auction website: https://izsoles.ta.gov.lv.</p><p>The auction takes place electronically at: https://izsoles.ta.gov.lv.</p><p>The Liepāja SEZ Authority first consolidated all properties on the site of the former Liepājas metalurgs plant, worked with the municipality to develop a local spatial plan, and constructed the first streets with the necessary utilities. Selling properties through auctions is the next step in involving entrepreneurs in regenerating and transforming the industrial site. It offers them the opportunity to acquire existing production buildings with land and renovate or reconstruct them to meet the requirements of a modern green-economy business environment.</p><p>The Liepāja Industrial Park is located in the Liepāja Special Economic Zone. It is intended for modern manufacturing, science and research, logistics centres and energy-intensive projects. The development area of approximately 120 hectares is divided into plots with building opportunities and access to utilities.</p><p>The Liepāja Industrial Park is being developed by the Liepāja SEZ Authority and Liepāja City Municipality on the former Liepājas metalurgs site between Brīvības, Meldru, Ezermalas, Parka and Zemnieku streets in Liepāja. It borders Lake Liepāja, a specially protected Natura 2000 site. Under the approved development strategy, the aim is to attract more than EUR 275 million in private investment and create at least 1,500 new jobs. Sustainability is embedded in the industrial park’s guiding principles, with a clear focus on education, innovation and the circular economy.</p></div>
